Town phase 1b done (claude/town-phase1b, from origin/claude/town-phase1a, origin/main a04bf0e9 merged in). PR title and body:
.pr-body.md. No PR opened, so CI has not run (it runs on a PR): the director opens it, with the `full-e2e` label. About 1 h 45 min.

What it does
- The town loads the build's baked pictures on every visit: the manifest (named by its contents; the app is handed the name as
  __TOWN_PICTURES__) and its town's pages fetched, decoded off the main thread, uploaded whole (town/baked.ts, town/baked-files.ts,
  town/manifest.ts; paint-gl.ts adopt places each file on the atlas's layers). Frame counts, roofs, glows and tops from the manifest.
- The service worker keeps the files (answered from any version's cache, copied to a new version as it installs). Home fetches them when
  idle (4 s after it shows, a file at a time, low priority; settings.ts TOWN_PICTURES.homeFetchAfterMs). The dev server bakes.
- Load first, then show: unchanged. The card lifts after every file is uploaded and the warm-up frames have settled.
- Same pixels: baked and painted, a player's town n 2250, hash 81fb216, gpu 8f62dba3; an admin's 2398, 76475003, c432b637 (phase 1a's).

Measured (headless Chromium, 4 cores, software WebGL; the tap on Chess Town until the town shows, timed in the page; 3 runs each)
- Slowed phone (iPhone 13, CPU 4x): first visit 11.0 to 11.3 s -> 3.4 to 4.4 s; later visit 3.9 to 4.2 -> 3.3 to 3.6 s; the first visit
  after a deploy (the same town built under another commit id, the same browser profile) 3.9 s, all 36 files already in the new
  version's cache, copied as its worker installed.
- Computer (1280 x 800, full speed): first 4.8 s -> 1.1 to 1.4 s; later 1.2 to 1.4 -> 1.0 to 1.4 s; after a deploy 1.3 s.
  "Before" is this branch with TOWN_PICTURES.baked off (the device paints, then keeps), on the same machine and probe.
- Bytes on a first visit: a player's town 35 files, 2.33 MB, and the manifest, 369 KB (56 KB gzipped); an admin's 40 files, 2.52 MB.
- Freezes on the loading screen (slowed): one task over 200 ms is left, the warm-up's first frame (its draw and the wait for the GPU,
  0.26 to 0.35 s, the bar full by then); before, 5 to 6 of up to 0.4 s. The longest task before the card shows: 0.3 to 0.6 s (was 1.2 to 1.4 s).
- Our frame's script cost (the held frame drawn 200 times, slowed, 4 runs in turn): 14.6 ms; before 14.4 on a first visit, 14.9 on a later one.

Split off, for phase 1c (not done here)
- The sidekicks' sheets are still fetched from the app's own assets and cut on the device (875 canvases, each uploaded alone: 0.17 s of
  a slowed load, and their uploads). They can't be adopted as they are: a frame has only 0 to 2 clear pixels at its edge, so a
  smoothed draw would read its neighbor. Bake each frame as a picture of its own (padded, as the rest). One wrinkle: render.ts finds
  a sheet's file by its id ("sidekick-beaver" -> "beaver"), and Rivet's file is timber.png, so an admin's town never draws him (phase
  1a's note). Baked by their names in SIDEKICK_SHEETS he would appear: a visible change, with a still. The manifest's `sheets` and
  the sheet files are unread until then (manifest.ts filesOf leaves them out).

For phase 1c to know
- The fallback is all or nothing: a file missing, ?paintall, or TOWN_PICTURES.baked off paints on the device. In a build with a baked
  town nothing is read from or kept in IndexedDB any more. To delete: paint-pool.ts and its worker, keep-pictures.ts's save and
  restore (its Pictures, PageIO and packPictures stay: baked.ts and the bake use them), the "hunchess-town" database on devices (5.8
  MB each, dead now), town-art.ts and __TOWN_ART__, the brc.townTops key, ?paintall / ?paintworkers / ?paintslow, TOWN_PAINT_WORKERS.
- With no fallback, a missing file needs an answer of its own: a tab left open across a deploy whose town files were never fetched
  gets the app's page for them (baked-files.ts rejects it). Reload as a stale chunk does (stale.ts), or the "didn't load" card.
- Budgets to measure again in e2e/perf.spec.ts: TOWN_LOAD_REFS 16 (now 5.9), TOWN_LONG_REFS, TOWN_KEPT_REFS 6 (4.7); I added
  TOWN_BAKED_FIRST_REFS 8 (5.9 to 6.0) so the first visit's check isn't on the edge.
- What's left of a slowed load (2.6 to 3.3 s): the files 0.6 to 0.9 s (the main thread mostly idle: the labels and sidekicks could be
  made meanwhile), uploading 0.6 to 0.9 s (software WebGL here: a phone's GPU will differ), the labels 0.23 s (phase 2), the
  sidekicks 0.17 s, the warm-up 0.4 to 0.5 s. Before the card: the town's code starting 0.2 to 0.3 s, then its start 0.3 to 0.6 s
  (makeTownArt's streetBoxes 80 ms, the rest spread).
- The decoded pages stay in memory until the town closes, as a later visit's did (36 M pixels, about 144 MB by arithmetic).
- A stand-in canvas is cut when a 2D context draws from it (keep-pictures.ts cutBeforeDraw wraps drawImage): on every visit now, as
  on later visits before.
- Dev: the app is handed "order.json" (it names the latest bake's manifest); the dev server bakes when /town-pictures/ is first asked
  for and again after a source of the pictures changes (vite.config.ts townPictures). Not as it starts: every frames:* script starts one.
- No _headers for /town-pictures/: without the service worker the browser asks the server again for each file (a 304).

Noticed, not changed
- This container's Chromium is newer than the repo's Playwright 1.56.1 expects (build 1243, not 1194): local e2e ran through a config
  of its own pointing at it, not committed. CI is unaffected.
- After it's live: Eric's /town?report on his phone and laptop (the phases' ask); GPU upload times couldn't be measured here.
